Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Provides: iio-sensor-proxy
Conflicts: iio-sensor-proxy
Replaces: iio-sensor-proxy
Description: IIO sensors to D-Bus proxy (Qualcomm SSC support)
 iio-sensor-proxy 3.9 built with -Dssc-support=enabled, which adds the sensors
 that Qualcomm's Sensor Core serves over QRTR/QMI through libssc to the usual
 IIO ones, and exports all of them on D-Bus as net.hadess.SensorProxy.
 .
 The archive build of iio-sensor-proxy cannot enable SSC support because libssc
 is not packaged in Debian or Ubuntu, so this is the SSC-capable variant. It
 declares that it provides, replaces and conflicts with iio-sensor-proxy, and
 the two must not be installed at the same time (they ship the same files).
 .
 Everything else is stock upstream 3.9: same D-Bus name, same unit name
 (iio-sensor-proxy.service, which marble-device-support drops in on) and the
 same file layout, so it is a drop-in replacement for the archive package.
 .
 Build-Depends on libssc is satisfied by this repository's own libssc package,
 which the build workflow installs before building this one; there is no libssc
 in the Debian archive, so a plain Debian build host needs libssc installed
 (or `dpkg-buildpackage -d`).
